IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Row il-71, TARGETED: the Severance Pay Law, 5723-1963 ("the Law"). Draft, target compiler main. No domain expert has read this against the source.
-- THIS ROW DOES NOT ENCODE THE LAW. It records two items (I1 and I2), each a reference whose target an amending instrument changed, as typed values, and tests them.
-- SEAT: the employee whose resignation subsection 11(ג) or 11(ה) treats as dismissal, in the places where those subsections apply. A row of references asks that individual no question: there is no input to ask for, and no @export.
-- NOUNS: an instrument of Sefer HaChukim, a place in the Law, an instruction an instrument prints, a text as an instrument printed it, a pointer inside a paragraph, a general word replacement, a commencement as the page prints it, an item, and the questions asked of them.
-- No reference is stated here; they are in sv71-cross-references.l4.
--
-- Every item is recorded with two limbs, as in the other targeted rows:
--   limb (a): the target is repealed, missing or says something else, read from an official instrument;
--   limb (b): the citing words still read so in the latest official instrument read.
-- Subsection letters are written with Latin names for the Hebrew letters the Law uses: (ג) is Gimel, (ד) Dalet, (ה) He, (ו) Vav, (א) Alef.
-- THE NAMES BELOW ARE MINE, not the Law's. A date typed as an issue date is the date the footer of the issue prints; it is NOT a commencement date.
-- A commencement is typed separately, and only where a page prints one.

§ `Nouns`

DECLARE `A way a fact was read` IS ONE OF
    `official page image`
    `official page image, with the consolidation agreeing (CONSOLIDATION-ONLY)`
    `official page image, with the later instruments listed in NOTES.md`
    `computed from the issue date, not printed`
    `CONSOLIDATION-ONLY`
    `not checked`

DECLARE `A subsection letter` IS ONE OF
    Alef
    Bet
    Gimel
    Dalet
    He
    Vav

DECLARE `A kind of instruction` IS ONE OF
    Insert
    Replace
    Delete
    `Replace words`
    `Delete words`

-- An issue of Sefer HaChukim. The issue date is the one the footer prints.
DECLARE `An instrument` HAS
    `its issue of Sefer HaChukim` IS A NUMBER
    `its issue date` IS A DATE

-- A place in the Law: a section, optionally a subsection, optionally a paragraph of it.
DECLARE `A place in the Law` HAS
    `its section` IS A NUMBER
    `its subsection` IS A MAYBE `A subsection letter`
    `its paragraph` IS A MAYBE NUMBER

-- An instruction an instrument prints about the Law.
-- `the words it names` are the words the instruction itself prints as replaced or deleted, `the words it puts` those it prints as put in; both are copied from the ext: line above the value.
DECLARE `An instruction` HAS
    `the instrument` IS AN `An instrument`
    `the printed page it is on` IS A NUMBER
    `the kind` IS A `A kind of instruction`
    `the place it names` IS A `A place in the Law`
    `it comes after the paragraph` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `it comes after the subsection` IS A MAYBE `A subsection letter`
    `the words it names` IS A LIST OF STRING
    `the words it puts` IS A LIST OF STRING
    `a page image of it is deposited` IS A BOOLEAN

-- An instruction an instrument prints about a law other than the Law. The place is given in words only; the row tests no place of another law.
DECLARE `An instruction on another law` HAS
    `the instrument` IS AN `An instrument`
    `the printed page it is on` IS A NUMBER
    `the law it amends` IS A STRING
    `the place it names, in words` IS A STRING
    `the kind` IS A `A kind of instruction`
    `the words it names` IS A LIST OF STRING
    `the words it puts` IS A LIST OF STRING
    `the page prints the words it removes` IS A BOOLEAN

-- A text as an instrument printed it: a paragraph, a subsection or a section of the Law.
DECLARE `A printed text` HAS
    `the instrument that printed it` IS AN `An instrument`
    `the printed page it is on` IS A NUMBER
    `the place it is printed at` IS A `A place in the Law`
    `its words` IS A STRING

-- A pointer inside a paragraph to another paragraph of the same subsection.
DECLARE `A pointer between paragraphs` HAS
    `the printed text that holds it` IS A `A printed text`
    `the pointer's words` IS A STRING
    `the term the pointer's words put in marks` IS A STRING
    `the paragraph the pointer names` IS A NUMBER
    `the named paragraph as the last instrument deposited here left it` IS A `A printed text`

DECLARE `A pair of words` HAS
    `the words replaced` IS A STRING
    `the words put in` IS A STRING

-- A general word replacement: an instrument that replaces words "in every place" in the laws of its Schedule. It names no section of the Law.
DECLARE `A general replacement` HAS
    `the instrument` IS AN `An instrument`
    `the printed page of the instruction` IS A NUMBER
    `the printed page of the Schedule` IS A NUMBER
    `the Schedule item that names the Law` IS A NUMBER
    `the pairs printed in the deposited band` IS A LIST OF `A pair of words`
    `the word the Schedule item excepts` IS A STRING
    `the section the exception is in` IS A NUMBER
    `it names a section of the Law` IS A BOOLEAN

-- A commencement as read. The date is typed only where the page prints a calendar date; otherwise the number of days the page prints, or nothing.
DECLARE `A commencement as read` HAS
    `the instrument` IS AN `An instrument`
    `the date the page prints` IS A MAYBE DATE
    `the number of days after publication the page prints` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `how it was read` IS A `A way a fact was read`

-- An item of the row, with its two limbs.
DECLARE `An item` HAS
    `the item` IS A STRING
    `the citing words are in` IS A STRING
    `limb (a) holds` IS A BOOLEAN
    `limb (a) was read` IS A `A way a fact was read`
    `limb (b) holds` IS A BOOLEAN
    `limb (b) was read` IS A `A way a fact was read`
    `the instruments and pages read` IS A STRING

-- ===== QUESTIONS ASKED OF THE VALUES =====

GIVEN t IS A `A printed text`, w IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the printed text contains the words` MEANS CONTAINS (t's `its words`) w

-- I1: does the paragraph a pointer names, as the last instrument deposited here left it, contain the term the pointer's own words put in marks?
GIVEN p IS A `A pointer between paragraphs`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the paragraph the pointer names contains the term in marks` MEANS
    CONTAINS (p's `the named paragraph as the last instrument deposited here left it`'s `its words`) (p's `the term the pointer's words put in marks`)

GIVEN p IS A `A pointer between paragraphs`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the pointer's words are among the words of the text that holds it` MEANS
    CONTAINS (p's `the printed text that holds it`'s `its words`) (p's `the pointer's words`)

GIVEN i IS AN `An instruction`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the instruction leaves the named paragraph in place` MEANS NOT (i's `the kind` EQUALS Delete)

GIVEN a IS AN `An instrument`, b IS AN `An instrument`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the first instrument was issued after the second` MEANS a's `its issue date` > b's `its issue date`

GIVEN a IS AN `An instrument`, b IS AN `An instrument`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the two instruments are two different issues` MEANS NOT (a's `its issue of Sefer HaChukim` EQUALS b's `its issue of Sefer HaChukim`)

GIVEN pl IS A `A place in the Law`, is IS A LIST OF `An instruction`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`some instruction in the list names the place` MEANS any (GIVEN i YIELD i's `the place it names` EQUALS pl) is

-- I2: is the phrase, written into a text of the Law by one instrument, replaced at that place by a later instruction in the list?
-- The instruction replaces words, names the place the text is printed at, names the phrase among the words it replaces, and was issued after the instrument that wrote the phrase.
GIVEN phrase IS A STRING, wr IS A `A printed text`, i IS AN `An instruction`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the instruction replaces the phrase at the place the text is printed at` MEANS
    (i's `the kind` EQUALS `Replace words`)
    AND (i's `the place it names` EQUALS wr's `the place it is printed at`)
    AND (elem phrase (i's `the words it names`))
    AND ((wr's `the instrument that printed it`)'s `its issue date` < (i's `the instrument`)'s `its issue date`)

GIVEN phrase IS A STRING, wr IS A `A printed text`, is IS A LIST OF `An instruction`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the phrase written in the text is replaced at that place by a later instruction` MEANS
    (CONTAINS (wr's `its words`) phrase)
    AND (any (GIVEN i YIELD `the instruction replaces the phrase at the place the text is printed at` phrase wr i) is)

-- None of the words an instruction names occurs inside the phrase.
GIVEN phrase IS A STRING, i IS AN `An instruction`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`no words the instruction names occur inside the phrase` MEANS all (GIVEN w YIELD NOT (CONTAINS phrase w)) (i's `the words it names`)

GIVEN phrase IS A STRING, g IS A `A general replacement`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`no words the general replacement names occur inside the phrase` MEANS
    all (GIVEN pr YIELD NOT (CONTAINS phrase (pr's `the words replaced`))) (g's `the pairs printed in the deposited band`)

-- The days a page prints, counted from the issue date. COMPUTED, NOT PRINTED: the page prints a number of days, never a calendar date.
GIVEN d IS A DATE, days IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the issue date plus the days, computed` MEANS DATE_FROM_SERIAL (DATE_SERIAL d PLUS days)

GIVEN c IS A `A commencement as read`
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the commencement date computed from the days the page prints` MEANS
    CONSIDER c's `the number of days after publication the page prints`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST n THEN JUST (`the issue date plus the days, computed` (c's `the instrument`'s `its issue date`) n)

GIVEN c IS AN `An item`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`both limbs hold` MEANS c's `limb (a) holds` AND c's `limb (b) holds`
